sequenceDiagram
  %% process.start on the Gateway engine: one `process` family on the Process's Node, one desired-state primitive, `process.ensure_state`, for a host systemd unit and a host Docker container (ADR 0267, ADR 0271; ProcessControlEngineFlow). Runtime proof on a nested fleet is pending.
  %% Covered: host systemd units and host Docker containers. A unit in an Instance container stays on Swamp: Swamp first moves the container's app account with a script, which no fixed argv reproduces, so the engine refuses it at admission (EngineUnsupported).
  %% status: built
  %% command: process:start
  %% kind: process.start
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Target Node<br/>executor
  CLI->>GW: process:start 417
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>Process 417: provisioning
  %%> Same admission as process/start.mmd: access to the Process's Node, a Process not being removed; the intent carries unit or container name, runtime, on-demand flag and Instance container
  opt drain-waiting, dev-server, release or container plan
    Note over GW: Refuse the engine<br/>EngineUnsupported
    %%> - the same drain-waiting Processes as process/engine/stop.mmd, so one Process never splits its lifecycle across engines: a host systemd Process that runs Horizon (`GatewayHorizon::runs` with no Instance, whose unit carries the long-drain stop directives of SystemdProcessRenderer) and a Gateway release-container Process (Horizon, the scheduler)
    %%> - a Vite dev Process (`vite_plan`: dev route, listener, awake marker) and a production release layout
    %%> - decided from the Process and its placement, for both verbs, never from start-only intent fields: a `vp-dev` or `vite` Process, a Process of an Instance not placed on app-dev, any intent with a `container` (an Instance container, whose app-account move is a script, or a Gateway release container), and a Node's host systemd unit that runs Horizon (the renderer's own drain condition: `GatewayHorizon::runs` on a Node Process; a Process named like a Gateway one, an Instance's Horizon unit and a Docker Horizon Process carry no long-drain directives and stay eligible)
    %%> - decided from the Gateway's own Node roles, never from the agent version or the Node's report: a Process on a Node not placed in development (an app-prod Node, both app roles or neither, no Node row) and an intent with `production_control` stay on Swamp
    %%> - decided at admission, before any order: the engine admits nothing, and the whole Operation takes the Swamp branch below
  end
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `process.start` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: the `process` family's desired-state action (one name for start and stop)
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    %%> - eligible plans: a host systemd unit or a host Docker container of a Node Process or an app-dev Instance Process
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock `process:<id>` commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    %%> - binding refuses `operation.target_busy` while another open Operation, on either engine, acts on the Process; while the lock is held, admission of any other Process verb refuses `operation.target_busy`
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    alt host systemd unit
      EN->>N: Converge the unit<br/>running · boot policy
      %%> Desired state: the unit is running and enabled at boot unless on-demand, as Swamp's `Set boot policy` / `Stop the Process` applies it; the admitted boot policy is an input of the step; an already-running unit only gets its boot policy
      %%> Target: the Process (`process-<id>`), so two orders for one Process run one after the other
    else Docker container
      EN->>N: Converge the container<br/>docker start · running
      %%> `docker container start` only when the state differs; an already-running container changes nothing
    end
    alt host systemd unit
      N-->>EN: Observed state<br/>loaded · active · boot policy
      %%> Read-back: LoadState=loaded, ActiveState=active, and UnitFileState=enabled for a persistent Process, disabled for an on-demand one (the admitted `on_demand`)
    else Docker container
      N-->>EN: Observed state<br/>State.Status running
      %%> Read-back: `docker container inspect` of the exact saved name answers that name, State.Status `running` and the admitted image
    end
    %%> A read that systemd answers without one of LoadState, ActiveState, SubState or UnitFileState never counts as that value: the step fails
    %%> The step fails with a code for its phase: the change (`process.input_invalid`, `process.unit_missing`, `process.container_missing`, `process.apply_failed`), a stop's plain `systemctl stop` after it (`process.unit_stop_failed`), the read-back read (`process.read_failed`), or a read that answered another state (`process.state_mismatch`); success is projected only from this read-back
    %%> The Operation records what Swamp's failed native check records: `operation.native_failed`, with the Swamp step the phase stands for as its failed step: `Start the Process` / `Stop the Process` or `Start the container` / `Stop the container` for the change, `Stop the unit`, `Check the unit` or `Check the container` for the read, `Verify the state` for the assert; a cancel records no error code, as a cancelled Swamp run does; the step's own code stays on the engine step and in the failure's detail
    %%> `applied` is 0 when nothing changed, so a repeat after a crash reports the same end state
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so Process 417 stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
      N-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Record Process running<br/>desired state · status
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Mark the Process failed<br/>desired state unchanged
      %%> - no rollback and nothing to clean up; the same command converges again after the cause is fixed
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-process-start
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-process-start (process/start.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
